{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread","id":1426200,"title":"RWBY Volume 8 Thread","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-11-25T21:32:52-08:00","id":1426200,"title":"RWBY Volume 8 Thread","content":"<span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Our heroes' worst fears have finally been realized: Salem is here, and the timing couldn't be worse for the divided Kingdom of Atlas. Fear has turned friends into enemies, while doubt threatens to splinter humanity's remaining allies. With both Salem and Ironwood stacking the odds against them, and the fate of Remnant at stake, it's up to team RWBY to make their play before it's too late.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12378-fma245","name":"FMA245","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"165"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-26T02:02:58-08:00","id":1426213,"title":"","content":"Why is this in exalted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-26T03:20:21-08:00","id":1426217,"title":"","content":"Always has been, essentially.<br /> (and that is asked every time too <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> <br /> RT is grounded, so I'm not going to give them the time of the day for now, but I hope they can continue on the quality increase from last volume.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-26T03:23:40-08:00","id":1426218,"title":"","content":"Well, I love the transforming weapons! <br /> <br /> And should probably try to create a Dust subsystem or thaumaturgical ritual .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-26T04:37:12-08:00","id":1426224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1426218#post1426218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I love the transforming weapons!<br /> <br /> And should probably try to create a Dust subsystem or thaumaturgical ritual .</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be a really cool idea. I know we already have 'Firedust', but I'm unsure if Exalted has other types of elemental dusts.<br /> <br /> As for how things are currently going in the series, it's shaping up to be quite cool. I'm wondering if the reason Salem is waiting is around is because she wants Atlas to willingly give themselves over to her- sort of like what the Mask of Winters did with Thorns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-26T04:52:31-08:00","id":1426225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Distant Choir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1426224#post1426224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be a really cool idea. I know we already have 'Firedust', but I'm unsure if Exalted has other types of elemental dusts.</div> </div> </div> </div>There... are. <br /> <br /> In the miracles of the solar exalted, but they're pretty much different types of gunpowder. Really boring. <br /> <br /> I say there should be a subsystem. A kind of pseudo artifact like those little gem thingies you can use. Maybe somewhat like those crystals Hansel can use. A alchemical ritual can turn them into expendable fuel for magitech machines, turning the world into somewhat final fantasy-esque. A willpower expenditure/ commitment allows the wearer to use elemental effects, with the difficulty based on the application (grabbing a crystal and using it will require a difficulty 4 roll. Using a catridge and firewand full of fire dust to use as a fireball spell equivalent is difficulty 1). <br /> <br /> Of course some may object to turning the world into final fantasy-esque, but I say you should ignore those people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-28T23:13:07-08:00","id":1426540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1426225#post1426225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There... are. <br /> <br /> In the miracles of the solar exalted, but they're pretty much different types of gunpowder. Really boring. <br /> <br /> I say there should be a subsystem. A kind of pseudo artifact like those little gem thingies you can use. Maybe somewhat like those crystals Hansel can use. A alchemical ritual can turn them into expendable fuel for magitech machines, turning the world into somewhat final fantasy-esque. A willpower expenditure/ commitment allows the wearer to use elemental effects, with the difficulty based on the application (grabbing a crystal and using it will require a difficulty 4 roll. Using a catridge and firewand full of fire dust to use as a fireball spell equivalent is difficulty 1). <br /> <br /> Of course some may object to turning the world into final fantasy-esque, but I say you should ignore those people.</div> </div> </div> </div>I went looking for this and i went to the Discord and I still have no idea what you mean. What powder? Where is it in Miracles?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-29T02:13:17-08:00","id":1426549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1426540#post1426540\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I went looking for this and i went to the Discord and I still have no idea what you mean. What powder? Where is it in Miracles?</div> </div> </div> </div>Check 2e in stead of 3e?<br /> <br /> edit: You know what? Ignore that. Tomorrow morning I'll grab my copy and try to copy it here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","user":"Accelerator","date":". 11-29-2020, 05:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T05:15:22-08:00","id":1426685,"title":"","content":"I imagine the Dusts in Exalted would perhaps be more diverse in powers even if there's fewer variants, since I think the force of Gravity comes under 'Earth' and Ice would come under 'Air'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T10:34:49-08:00","id":1426722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Distant Choir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1426685#post1426685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine the Dusts in Exalted would perhaps be more diverse in powers even if there's fewer variants, since I think the force of Gravity comes under 'Earth' and Ice would come under 'Air'.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Water Dust&quot; would still seem pretty underwhelming.<br /> <br /> Fire Dust is super-coal, or jet fuel.<br /> <br /> Earth Dust is like super-concrete. Make solid stone in any shape you need; great for solid construction that lasts for centuries.<br /> <br /> Air Dust can be used for pseudo-steam engines or air-jet fuel.<br /> <br /> Wood Dust can be used, presumably, for wooden construction in a similar way to Earth Dust and stone construction, but also probably used for producing rare plants for medicinal purposes, or crop plants for harvests.<br /> <br /> Water Dust would mostly be a different way to transport and store potable water. Very important in arid regions, and virtually useless anywhere else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T13:44:20-08:00","id":1426735,"title":"","content":"What about cooling down machinery or as blasts of disintegration? After all, water is the universal solvent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T15:22:02-08:00","id":1426748,"title":"","content":"Remember, there's more than just TERRESTRIAL Elements in Creation.<br /> <br /> Hard Light Dust may be like, Solar-Aligned Dust or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T16:37:50-08:00","id":1426758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1426748#post1426748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember, there's more than just TERRESTRIAL Elements in Creation.<br /> <br /> Hard Light Dust may be like, Solar-Aligned Dust or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh boy. What about Abyssal and Lunar and Sidereal? <br /> <br /> this can be some pretty good worldbuilding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T18:27:32-08:00","id":1426777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1426735#post1426735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about cooling down machinery or as blasts of disintegration? After all, water is the universal solvent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, Elemental Dust could be used for less obvious manifestations, but using Water Dust to produce acid would require a skill that most people wouldn\u2019t cultivate. If you just mechanically ignite Water Dust, you\u2019re getting ordinary water.<br /> <br /> As for using water as coolant, few communities in Creation have machines that require coolant. For those that do, they can use regular water for that. If you\u2019re not in the South, plain old water is plentiful enough. If you are in the South, you have more urgent uses for water.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1426758#post1426758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh boy. What about Abyssal and Lunar and Sidereal?<br /> <br /> this can be some pretty good worldbuilding.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the spires of purple Dust around Salem\u2019s castle aren\u2019t the Gravity Dust she used for her whale-carrier, then it could be Abyssal Dust.<br /> <br /> Actually, Salem works really well as a Death Lord. Angry, hateful, super-powerful ghost that cannot be destroyed unless you fulfill her one weakness. Which in her case, is getting over herself and admitting that she isn\u2019t the center of the universe and that other people are her equals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T21:04:02-08:00","id":1426794,"title":"","content":"If Salem were a Deathloed then her 4 lieutenants would be her Abyssals.<br /> <br /> Hazel=Dusk<br /> Watts=Daybreak<br /> Tyrian=Day<br /> Cinder=Moonshadow<br /> <br /> Mercury Emerald and Neo are just mortals Cinder talked into helping her","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T07:19:39-08:00","id":1426825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1426794#post1426794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Salem were a Deathloed then her 4 lieutenants would be her Abyssals.<br /> <br /> Hazel=Dusk<br /> Watts=Daybreak<br /> Tyrian=Day<br /> Cinder=Moonshadow<br /> <br /> Mercury Emerald and Neo are just mortals Cinder talked into helping her</div> </div> </div> </div>Mercury, Emerald, and Neo are Terrestrial Exalted at the very least.<br /> <br /> Salem's other minions could be any sort of Exalt she recruited.<br /> <br /> Particularly Watts, who owes the least to Salem. She hasn't granted him anything but an opportunity to hurt Ironwood. His story is all about how he owes his own genius to no one but himself and everyone should worship him for his intellectual godhood.<br /> <br /> Cinder is the total opposite, since apparently every form of power she has comes from Salem in some way. Even her own Aura and Semblance, while inherent to herself, probably benefited from Salem's training or any tutors she provided. The Grimm parasite in particular ties her to Salem in a way vaguely reminiscent of an Abyssal Monstrance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T16:27:04-08:00","id":1426878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1426825#post1426825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mercury, Emerald, and Neo are Terrestrial Exalted at the very least.<br /> <br /> Salem's other minions could be any sort of Exalt she recruited.</div> </div> </div> </div>Power Tier is a bit odd with porting RWBY to Creation, because like... Is Emerald a Terrestrial? Is she some kind of God Blood or Exigent with a VERY good trick of Mental Illusions?<br /> <br /> Would Aura-users be roughly akin to what 2e considered to be Enlightened Mortals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T18:36:08-08:00","id":1426891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1426878#post1426878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Power Tier is a bit odd with porting RWBY to Creation, because like... Is Emerald a Terrestrial? Is she some kind of God Blood or Exigent with a VERY good trick of Mental Illusions?<br /> <br /> Would Aura-users be roughly akin to what 2e considered to be Enlightened Mortals?</div> </div> </div> </div>In general, I think Huntsmen are Terrestrial level, and modeling them as Terrestrial Exalted works well with the potential for being a Huntsman being hereditary.<br /> <br /> The Branwen / Xiao Long / Rose family is a small house of Fire Aspects.<br /> <br /> Jaune and Weiss have long legacies of power.<br /> <br /> Lie Ren and Nora are Lost Eggs.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for Emerald, didn\u2019t Terrestrial Performance get a powerful illusionary Water Signature Charm?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T20:49:00-08:00","id":1426909,"title":"","content":"Putting my vote behind Cinder as Midnight Caste. She's drank the dark juice and regurgitated it, less 'enjoy my superior undead culture, foreigners'. <br /> <br /> The first three episodes have been great. RT's site has them, of course, but Crunchyroll has 'em as well.<br /> <br /> I get that Salem is waiting to open the relic of knowledge before proceeding because she thinks her current position is unassailable. I suppose immortals just aren't in a hurry?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T22:38:18-08:00","id":1426922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1426909#post1426909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get that Salem is waiting to open the relic of knowledge before proceeding because she thinks her current position is unassailable. I suppose immortals just aren't in a hurry?</div> </div> </div> </div>Atlas and Mantle are mostly inconsequential to her. The important thing is the Relic. She has a massive Grimm army engaging in a passive siege. She doesn't need to charge in and crush them all, she can just outlast them. Grimm don't need to eat, don't need to sleep, they don't need Dust or Aura to survive in the tundra... Honestly it's to her advantage to just wait until she has the knowledge she needs, to get her pieces in order, and then make a move for the Staff of Creation.<br /> <br /> (And that is why I roll my eyes at the people who go &quot;Why is Salem just waiting? SHIT WRITING, RT!&quot;)<br /> <br /> As for Cinder... She could be some kind of Deathknight if you make Salem a Deathlord... But I think that honestly, Cinder's entire Thing fits more as some kind of Infernal. What little we know of her, anyway. Consider:<br /> <br /> RT has said that most of Salem's lieutenants are... What Ifs.<br /> <br /> What If Watson were friends with a Moriarty instead of a Holmes for Watts.<br /> <br /> What If Hansel had lost Gretel, for Hazel.<br /> <br /> And Salem herself is &quot;What if Happily Ever After... Wasn't?&quot;<br /> <br /> I believe that Cinder is &quot;What if Cinderella's Fairy Godmother never came?&quot; And Cinder, from the scraps of his motivation we've seen, wants power. Wants to be feared. Wants to be able to crush people. We know from what she was yelling at Winter in V7 that she hates the Elite who hold power over others, and we saw that snippet of her washing floors... I could see Cinder either being a Deathknight (either a Midnight or maybe a Day) or as an Infernal, possibly as... Okay I think the new names for the Zenith-likes and Night-likes are... Ascendant and Nadir.<br /> <br /> Hm. Salem COULD be a very spooky Third Circle, or a human who was forcibly converted into a Third Circle, with the Grimm as types of Demons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1426891#post1426891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In general, I think Huntsmen are Terrestrial level, and modeling them as Terrestrial Exalted works well with the potential for being a Huntsman being hereditary.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean the slight problem with this is that Aura can be awoken from the outside. I don't think it's ENTIRELY hereditary, I think basically every human on Remnant (and a few animals) can get their Aura awoken.<br /> <br /> I won't argue that they're can't be roughly Terrestrial Tier, but I think the Silver Eyes are more bloodline-related than the ability to use Aura.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 12-02-2020, 01:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T06:53:12-08:00","id":1426970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1426922#post1426922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean the slight problem with this is that Aura can be awoken from the outside</div> </div> </div> </div>We have NEVER seen that happen again, and the concept damn near breaks the setting.<br /> <br /> It makes no sense that Jaune &quot;I grew up always wanting to be a Huntsman like my father&quot; Arc didn't even know what Aura is, in a world where the Vytal Tournament is a globally televised event where Aura is monitored like Health Bars and the announcers delight in explaining revealed Semblances to the audience.<br /> <br /> It makes more sense that Jaune knew what Aura is and learned how to use it in his normal high-school's athletics program, and what he really lacked was combat training.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think the Silver Eyes are more bloodline-related than the ability to use Aura. </div> </div> </div>The Silver Eyes are very much that &quot;you're an Exalt with one Eclipse-OK Charm because of your lineage&quot; Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T07:33:31-08:00","id":1426981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1426970#post1426970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We have NEVER seen that happen again, and the concept damn near breaks the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>'Breaks the setting'? That's a Take, and one I definitely disagree with. If you're pulling into the 'Why doesn't EVERYBODY get their Aura unlocked?'<br /> <br /> I dunno, why doesn't everyone in our world learn how to shoot a gun? Why doesn't everyone take some kind of combat course? Some people don't like fighting, even in a world like Remnant. And some people still need to make coffee in Vale. I figure most people on Remnant know how to shoot or something, but having one's Aura unlocked is going several steps beyond and making a commitment to dedicating your life to fighting Grimm (or being a bandit). Most people on Remnant aren't going to have unlocked Aura for the same reason that most people in our world don't go into special forces training.<br /> <br /> Plus, the second novel establishes that high Aura sources can also draw in the Grimm, in addition to negativity, so too much Aura in one place can be dangerous.<br /> <br /> ALSO also there's no indication that Jaune's immediate father is a Huntsman. He said that the Arc Family has a history of warriors, but it's very likely that there hasn't been a fighter in the family since his great grandfather, and that the Arcs are the Remnant version of Old Money. They were great warriors, once upon a time, but now they're not.<br /> <br /> And honestly I'm not surprised at the idea of some dumb teen wanting to be something and not thinking it through and not having anywhere near as much knowledge on the subject as he could.<br /> <br /> Also call me a bit crazy but I think I prefer &quot;Anybody can use their Aura with time, dedication, and maybe a kind mentor to help you unlock your potential&quot; than the tired-ass &quot;Ooooooooh Aura Use is in the bloodline&quot;<br /> <br /> Ren is an orphan from the middle of nowhere, as is Nora. His Aura unlocked under a moment of stress and desperation. His dad, by all indications, looked like a regular hunter. As in 'Hunts game for food'. Where's the indication of 'Huntsman Potential is in the blood' there?<br /> <br /> No, it makes much more sense that the Potential for unlocking Aura is in literally every person on Remnant.<br /> <br /> I think that if there's ANY tendency of families producing Huntsmen and Huntresses, it's social. Like how Monty once said about Semblances:<br /> <br /> &quot;[Family Semblances] usually aren't identical but they can be similar. Like how Tony Hawk's kids probably know a lot about skateboarding&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T08:29:18-08:00","id":1426987,"title":"","content":"What is the general consensus of the RWBY media outside the main series?<br /> <br /> I read the DC comics and a lot of them were...not great. I hear that they've recently made a second Manga that's supposed to patch together the early hectic seasons but I believe they stopped that for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T10:09:28-08:00","id":1426996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Distant Choir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1426987#post1426987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the general consensus of the RWBY media outside the main series?<br /> <br /> I read the DC comics and a lot of them were...not great. I hear that they've recently made a second Manga that's supposed to patch together the early hectic seasons but I believe they stopped that for now.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't read any of the comics, but I'll recommend After the Fall and Before the Dawn, the novels. The plots are basic but the character moments are great.<br /> <br /> And if you like the concept of in-universe fiction, I <i>really</i> recommend the Fairy Tales of Remnant book. Plus there's some fun cultural notes left by Ozpin between the chapters, which gets funny when one of the fairy tales in the book is CLEARLY about a previous Incarnation.<br /> <br /> (Ozpin takes a chance after THAT particular story to talk about how one must take the story<i>teller</i> into account, and whatever biases and agendas, whether intentional or not, the teller is putting into the story)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 12-02-2020, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T15:53:44-08:00","id":1427050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1426981#post1426981\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also call me a bit crazy but I think I prefer &quot;Anybody can use their Aura with time, dedication, and maybe a kind mentor to help you unlock your potential&quot; than the tired-ass &quot;Ooooooooh Aura Use is in the bloodline&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>So would I!<br /> <br /> I absolutely loved the idea that anyone could become a Huntsmen through hard work.<br /> <br /> But we don't get to change canon, which has introduced the facts that people like Jaune can be born with &quot;a lot&quot; of Aura, and people can be born with almost no Aura, and no one bats an eye about either.<br /> <br /> Though I think the weakling was ejected from the Academy because of his attitude rather than his aptitude.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus, the second novel establishes that high Aura sources can also draw in the Grimm, in addition to negativity, so too much Aura in one place can be dangerous. </div> </div> </div>Do you think Pyrrha <i>gave </i>Jaune his &quot;lot of&quot; Aura? Like, she actually reduced the amount of Aura she herself started with, like Pietro doing so to bring Penny to life?<br /> <br /> Pyrrha told Jaune &quot;You have a lot of it&quot;. As though it was the amount he already had, and just didn't know how to use.<br /> <br /> &quot;I used my Aura to unlock yours, but the energy that protects you now is your own.&quot; - Pyrrha, Volume 1, Chapter 6, &quot;The Emerald Forest&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Furthermore, the situation in Before The Dawn was unusual, in that all of those individuals who attracted the Grimm had more Aura than even Jaune normally has. It was an unnatural concentration of Aura that doesn't normally happen without a very specific Semblance enabling it.<br /> <br /> And most of that Aura was taken from civilians who had never learned how to use it. Because they still HAD Aura, one way or the other.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ALSO also there's no indication that Jaune's immediate father is a Huntsman. </div> </div> </div>&quot;He comes from a long line of Huntsmen&quot; -- RWBY Companion book, page 73<br /> <br /> &quot;My father, my grandfather, and his father before him were all warriors!&quot; - Jaune, Volume 1, Chapter 12, &quot;Jaundice, Part 2&quot;<br /> <br /> If Jaune only described his father as a &quot;hero&quot;, then you might have been able to argue he was a firefighter or policeman or EMT. But he called him a warrior, and the Companion book doesn't exclude his father from the &quot;long line&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T17:51:10-08:00","id":1427071,"title":"","content":"Can I just say I love the World of Remnant videos? They're so interesting. Should have more of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T22:20:35-08:00","id":1427103,"title":"","content":"If someone could meditate on you for 10 seconds and give unlock a forcefield shield that exists within every living being sans Grimm, and this is not a Dangerous Forbidden Technique or anything, then almost every person in the world would have it done to them as part of school/birthday milestones or likewise. There's no person who wouldn't benefit from &quot;don't get cut, bruised, or burnt&quot; during their daily life, and even though Pyrra is a World Class athlete there's nothing special about her doing the unlocking on screen. She does it in uder a minute, in the wild, with a man she just met. <br /> <br /> Its not the hugest plot hole ever, but in a worldbuilding sense there's no reason it wouldn't be part of general life for everyone. It'd be the Remnant equivalent of getting vaccines at school.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T22:41:21-08:00","id":1427105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1427071#post1427071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I just say I love the World of Remnant videos? They're so interesting. Should have more of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I happen to have written a <a href=\"https://archiveofourown.org/works/10223006\" target=\"_blank\">fan script </a>for a World of Remnant video, which you may enjoy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T22:48:13-08:00","id":1427106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Accelerator</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1427071#post1427071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can I just say I love the World of Remnant videos? They're so interesting. Should have more of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>The original reason for the WoR videos was that due to the previous production schedules, they would have had to take off weeks every so often. It was post nothing... Or post videos that were mostly minimal animation and exposition voiceover.<br /> <br /> That being said, yes, I too would like more WoR videos. Maybe between seasons. About entirely small things.<br /> <br /> Like the Philosophy of Weapons by Kingdoms, even things like &quot;In Mistral, many warriors view weapons as things that should be designed as works of art. Gilding and decoration are common. With Vacuo, by contrast, they value practical and hardy weapons above overly decorative collection pieces.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1427103#post1427103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If someone could meditate on you for 10 seconds and give unlock a forcefield shield that exists within every living being sans Grimm, and this is not a Dangerous Forbidden Technique or anything, then almost every person in the world would have it done to them as part of school/birthday milestones or likewise. There's no person who wouldn't benefit from &quot;don't get cut, bruised, or burnt&quot; during their daily life, and even though Pyrra is a World Class athlete there's nothing special about her doing the unlocking on screen. She does it in uder a minute, in the wild, with a man she just met.<br /> <br /> Its not the hugest plot hole ever, but in a worldbuilding sense there's no reason it wouldn't be part of general life for everyone. It'd be the Remnant equivalent of getting vaccines at school.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not everybody can afford <a href=\"https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/CI3mxhjXILVZE02Us9zg7ozWOZ5o-LCGBSpacB7qSnMoyFRnm_iNlVubwvdplTNIQg1Zx0HSR8d540ntauPq2Lg7xR8pnfsAtwj2ZsLvQJDfkS8_ZQyIHJ4n6tnZboGRbsYhcLqG\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter Portions</a> :P<br /> <br /> (Mostly being glib here, I don't got much else beyond &quot;Not everybody would want to learn how to fight&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 12-03-2020, 01:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T23:09:37-08:00","id":1427109,"title":"","content":"Like... here's the thing. Worldbuilding is hard. It's even harder to fit in good worldbuilding while talking about plot, characters, setting... that kind of thing. World of Remnant is something that can let you just goddamned infodump in everything into one single 5 minute video. With cool illustrations, even! Without slowing down the plot and not doing any kind of cringeworthy 'as you know' shit.<br /> <br /> We can even skip the plothole of Jaune thingy, by instead of having an idiot who doesn't know what Aura is (despite wanting to be a Huntsmen) we can just have an exposition video, and spend the entire time doing something else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T08:36:18-08:00","id":1427143,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sorcerous Overlord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1427103#post1427103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If someone could meditate on you for 10 seconds and give unlock a forcefield shield that exists within every living being sans Grimm, and this is not a Dangerous Forbidden Technique or anything, then almost every person in the world would have it done to them as part of school/birthday milestones or likewise. There's no person who wouldn't benefit from &quot;don't get cut, bruised, or burnt&quot; during their daily life, and even though Pyrra is a World Class athlete there's nothing special about her doing the unlocking on screen. She does it in uder a minute, in the wild, with a man she just met.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. Even for those who have tiny Aura reserves, some protection is better than none.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Its not the hugest plot hole ever, but in a worldbuilding sense there's no reason it wouldn't be part of general life for everyone. It'd be the Remnant equivalent of getting vaccines at school. </div> </div> </div>There's also the fact that no one performs the same technique on Oscar, not even Ozpin inside of him. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2142_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2142\" data-vbnamecard=\"2142\">Kyman201</a> <br /> <br /> Oscar has to learn how to use his Aura to protect himself by sparring bare-knuckled against Ruby until he learns how to make her punches hurt less.<br /> <br /> If the technique Pyrrha used really existed, they could find SOMEONE in Mistral (one of the furloughed professors of the academy?) to give Oscar the same headstart that Jaune got.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T10:02:08-08:00","id":1427159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1427143#post1427143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oscar has to learn how to use his Aura to protect himself by sparring bare-knuckled against Ruby until he learns how to make her punches hurt less.<br /> <br /> If the technique Pyrrha used really existed, they could find SOMEONE in Mistral (one of the furloughed professors of the academy?) to give Oscar the same headstart that Jaune got.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thaaaaat's not what those lessons were? Oscar's Aura was unlocked. Like there was no need to do the Unlock Aura thing. (His Aura may have awoken when Oz joined with him, maybe one of the other students gave a startup ignition off-screen and it wasn't important enough to show because it's really not since they showed it already back in V1)<br /> <br /> They were teaching him to get faster and better at putting it up. Like, Aura isn't a constant automatic protection and it never was, you gotta deploy it. You just need training until deployment is reflexive.<br /> <br /> They said that. With words. &quot;Soon you'll be able to deploy your Aura on reflex&quot; or something to that effect.<br /> <br /> Edit: Okay I don't know if you've ever done any actual combat training and I haven't done karate for a long time so it's been a bit, but like... Yeah, there was a lot of truth in that 'Okay now we're gonna teach you until you do it without thinking'. Do enough training and you'll start reflexively putting up your guard when you sense things are getting messy.<br /> <br /> Edit 2: Anyway, as noted, given how widespread the origins of various Huntsmen and Huntresses are even leaving out how easy it is to awaken another Aura, and how SPECIFIC each power is... While I've no doubt that an Aura-user from RWBY is definitely in the weight class of a Terrestrial I don't know if I'd make them Dragon-Bloods or the like. They'd probably need to be designed as something different, possibly using the Exigent rules.<br /> <br /> Though in a future game I would love to use Penny as an Alchemical. Heck, assuming the Atlas labs she definitely has the required infrastructure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 12-03-2020, 11:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-07T01:43:58-08:00","id":1427535,"title":"","content":"V8C5 basically:<br /> <br /> THE BEACONS OF MINAS TIRITH! THE BEACONS ARE LIT!<br /> <br /> Gondor calls for aid!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","user":"vampire hunter D","date":". 12-19-2020, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-08T13:58:48-08:00","id":1427750,"title":"","content":"Welp.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('