"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-08T04:03:00-08:00","id":1434828,"title":"","content":"the Grimm feel more like something out of Malpheas to me<br /> <br /> or, maybe that goop could be a sorcerous weapon of some kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-08T04:15:20-08:00","id":1434829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1434828#post1434828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Grimm feel more like something out of Malpheas to me<br /> <br /> or, maybe that goop could be a sorcerous weapon of some kind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Self-reproducing sorcerous weapon that fights like a 1st cd and can grow even bigger? What is this, a FAA weapon?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-11T13:45:21-08:00","id":1435245,"title":"","content":"Hm, the Grimm also evoke deathly/underworld Aesthetics, what with the visible bone plating. And apparently in one of the livestreams it was mentioned that Grimm Goo was, in the early planning days, a different substance that could <i>create</i> Grimm by pouring it on animals. Like a normal wolf would be transformed into a Beowolf by applying Grimm Goo.<br /> <br /> Maybe Grimm Goo could be some kind of Sorcerous or Necromantic weapon that corrupts that which it touches?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T15:14:51-08:00","id":1437289,"title":"","content":"So....um....what Essence level was that Evocation Oz/car just used?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T15:25:52-08:00","id":1437290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1437289#post1437289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So....um....what Essence level was that Evocation Oz/car just used?</div> </div> </div> </div>Whatever is appropriate for an Evocation that can only ever do something like that once, maybe twice, every thousand years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T16:58:25-08:00","id":1437297,"title":"","content":"See that's what happens when you try to get crafty with your homebrew Evocations.<br /> <br /> Your player goes &quot;Oh it's nothing major, it's just a Permanent power that lets me transfer one Initiative to the weapon itself each time I successfully inflict Withering damage on a target&quot; and then twenty sessions later they point out &quot;It's a PERMANENT Evocation with no cap and it doesn't say <i>This Initiative fades at the end of battle</i>. I've stored up over 100 Initiative over the course of this campaign&quot;<br /> <br /> Only, as Sunder noted, this one was built up over several lifetimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 02-27-2021, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T17:19:21-08:00","id":1437300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1437297#post1437297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See that's what happens when you try to get crafty with your homebrew Evocations.<br /> <br /> Your player goes &quot;Oh it's nothing major, it's just a Permanent power that lets me transfer one Initiative to the weapon itself each time I successfully inflict Withering damage on a target&quot; and then twenty sessions later they point out &quot;It's a PERMANENT Evocation with no cap and it doesn't say <i>This Initiative fades at the end of battle</i>. I've stored up over 100 Initiative over the course of this campaign&quot;<br /> <br /> Only, as Sunder noted, this one was built up over several lifetimes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen the concept done at least once before, but it's not the most popular weapon design, and certainly hasn't appeared in Exalted.<br /> <br /> The closest is the Immaculate myth of Hesiesh never using his Essence until the day came to incinerate the Anathema.<br /> <br /> The last time I can recall this concept coming up (in a Japanese franchise called <i>Accel World</i>) is a katana that continuously stores up power the longer it is sheathed, and which expends all of that power on a single strike without any ability to conserve. I think it was called Infinite Blade or Infinite Edge.<br /> <br /> Of course such a concept is unpopular; only the most self-restrained and patient of people would opt into this kind of weapon, and most of them would never actually use it because they'd always be fretting about the potential of needing that power MORE for some later challenge.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Which might be why Ozpin died to Cinder at Beacon when he had this kind of power at his disposal.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, while Ozpin COULD release less than the total amount of stored power, he couldn't unleash a small enough amount to be sure he wouldn't damage Beacon Tower above.<br /> <br /> The first time Oscar used this power, he used LESS than in this episode, and it was still enough to blow a hole into the floor the shaft he was falling down... a hole that piercing through the bottom of Atlas's foundation.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-27T22:47:05-07:00","id":1441750,"title":"","content":"So, now two questions: If I wanted to turn a Jade Alchemical into a Celestial Exalt, can I do that?<br /> <br /> What level working would it take to make the transit dimension?<br /> <br /> and lastly:<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">damn Cinder. I wanted her to be a candidate for redemtion. Then she did...<i>this</i></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-31T04:06:11-07:00","id":1442158,"title":"","content":"bumping this thread back up now that the forum is fixed.<br /> <br /> The last scene btw, feels like the fall of Tzatli doesn't it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-31T07:30:18-07:00","id":1442171,"title":"","content":"The Staff of Creation and its Spirit aren't on the level of the Eye of Autochthon, but it gives you a taste of the kind of power such an Artifact can grant you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-31T07:34:19-07:00","id":1442172,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1441750#post1441750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, now two questions: If I wanted to turn a Jade Alchemical into a Celestial Exalt, can I do that?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can do anything you want at your table, but if you want to follow the &quot;rules&quot;...<br /> <br /> Then it bears mentioning that &quot;Alchemical Exalt&quot; is not the only option for representing Penny. It's entirely possible for a sorceror-engineer to produce a robot girl with a soul and a number of traits and even Charms.<br /> <br /> First-Age-Artifice Penny wouldn't have the growth potential of an Exalt, but she could be made more than powerful enough to overshadow young Exalted, or even some veteran Exalted like General Ironwood.<br /> <br /> And if she's not an Exalt but has a human soul, then she's a viable candidate for Celestial or Exigent Exaltation, and a sorcerous working or powerful Artifact could transform her body from machine to animal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T18:56:48-07:00","id":1442569,"title":"","content":"Episode's out for everyone now, friends.<br /> <br /> How bad are we feeling?<br /> <br /> Feeling pretty bad, myself.<br /> <br /> <br /> Putting all that work into getting yourself an N/A Artifact and using to to conduct a sorcerous working to turn your recently-Exalted robot buddy/girlfriend into an Exalted human, only for her to die in the next session where you ALSO lose the Artifact?<br /> <br /> Feels bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-03T19:28:56-07:00","id":1442570,"title":"","content":"Does GSS make multiple blades like when Penny summoned her swords? Or should that be a custom cham building off it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T06:36:05-07:00","id":1442715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1442570#post1442570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does GSS make multiple blades like when Penny summoned her swords? Or should that be a custom cham building off it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mechanically, you can buy identical one-handed weapons as a set that counts as one weapon.<br /> <br /> Penny effectively has a pair of short swords/daiklaves, even if there's six of them. They're all identical, so none of them have any varying tags for her to exploit, and the only immediate advantage in a mechanical sense is the Clash bonus for paired weapons, and it being that much harder to disarm her.<br /> <br /> She would need to invest into specialized GSS upgrades/Evocations or a floating-blade Martial Art style to begin seeing any other real returns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-05T07:39:58-07:00","id":1442722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vampire hunter D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1442570#post1442570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does GSS make multiple blades like when Penny summoned her swords? Or should that be a custom cham building off it?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd look for the wings of blades or whatever style that the Lunar KS book will feature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-06T01:01:36-07:00","id":1442810,"title":"","content":"The heroes' journey continues into death, from which plot armor will save them. Still, I'm eager to watch how it will happen.<br /> <br /> Also, great goddess vibes on Winter.<br /> <br /> Regarding Alchemcial Exalts: they are already classed Celestial. But, like, through the magic of soulgems and new bodies, I'm sure you could homebrew an Alchemical-to-other Exaltation event.<br /> <br /> Salem will eventually collect all four relics, because that has the most potential for drama. So, halfway? 8 more seasons?!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-13T10:14:14-07:00","id":1443755,"title":"","content":"I think they were going for subverting expectations but a cool premise and an interesting set-up leading to a disappointing resolution is what I've come to expect from RWBY.<br /> <br /> I don't consider myself a hate watcher but at this point it's something I watch as a GM/storyteller to vivisect a season and see what they're doing wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-14T14:48:47-07:00","id":1443938,"title":"","content":"Ok, bad idea I just had regarding turning an Alchemical into another Celestial....<br /> <br /> What if something like that can be done...and in the process creates a new Exaltation Shard that will reincarnate upon death. Of course, it will be of the type corresponding to the Alchemical's Material (so no point to this for Jade).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1047,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","user":"vampire hunter D","date":". 04-15-2021, 02:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T17:01:28-07:00","id":1444094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1443755#post1443755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they were going for subverting expectations but a cool premise and an interesting set-up leading to a disappointing resolution is what I've come to expect from RWBY.<br /> <br /> I don't consider myself a hate watcher but at this point it's something I watch as a GM/storyteller to vivisect a season and see what they're doing wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>What\u2019s disappointing about it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-15T18:48:49-07:00","id":1444119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1444094#post1444094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What\u2019s disappointing about it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for a recent example. killing Penny was inherently disappointing for anyone who liked Penny and wanted to see how she'd be changed by a major metamorphosis like that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T15:37:12-07:00","id":1444394,"title":"","content":"Penny's story line is a jerk move on their part, honestly. I am kind of mad at how they kept jerking us around as to her eventual fate then killed her after all the trouble the cast went through to keep her alive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar988_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T18:31:29-07:00","id":1444421,"title":"","content":"They spent an coupe episodes setting up interesting ideas(Cinder learned the value of team work, Penny became a real girl) and then...kinda tossed both out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-17T22:00:53-07:00","id":1444443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1444421#post1444421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They spent an coupe episodes setting up interesting ideas(Cinder learned the value of team work, Penny became a real girl) and then...kinda tossed both out.</div> </div> </div> </div>All so we could have the Batman 1966 tier cliff-hanger of \u201cDid the show called RWBY just kill all of team RWBY?\u201d<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T01:54:12-07:00","id":1444462,"title":"","content":"They weren't going to kill Yang. Then when I saw others going off the sides I knew it was a fake out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T02:54:14-07:00","id":1444471,"title":"","content":"In some ways, it is unfortunate that they couldn't keep Penny around and that Cinder doubled down on being evil. On the other hand, I think it pushes the show in a very interesting direction that Penny is permanently dead, but at least went out on her own terms - no matter how under duress she was. I don't think the subversions here were all too bad, since the new stories they've just opened up from closing some older stories certainly pique my interest.<br /> <br /> Of course, the looming spectre of &quot;what if it's not as satisfying as I think in my head&quot; is a thing, but I have high hopes. The volumes have been steadily improving in quality since V5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T03:39:14-07:00","id":1444480,"title":"","content":"I want to clarify that I don't mean &quot;Cinder didn't go full Zuko and so I'm sad&quot;, but rather the idea of a villian realizing that team work and co-operation can benefit them and using that for evil was rather nice.<br /> But they had to kill the techy-dapper villian, Penny, toss Neo off a cliff, and scatter everyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T14:40:46-07:00","id":1444551,"title":"","content":"One of the things that stands out as off to me is Watt's getting played by Cinder and crashing with Atlas. He's been shown to be smarter than that, not putting up with Cinder's games, and always has a backup plan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T17:23:21-07:00","id":1444570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1444551#post1444551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the things that stands out as off to me is Watt's getting played by Cinder and crashing with Atlas. He's been shown to be smarter than that, not putting up with Cinder's games, and always has a backup plan.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's entirely possible there just wasn't much to be done. The whole place collapsed so his usual options would be limited. If she took a minute to nail his foot to the floor there's not much he could do.<br /> <br /> It is <i>also</i> entirely possible he did escape that, as in those circumstances a last-second escape would be reasonably within his reach just as well. We didn't see more than a couple minutes into the outcome of her petty revenge on him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 04-18-2021, 08:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T22:06:24-07:00","id":1444598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1444570#post1444570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's entirely possible there just wasn't much to be done. The whole place collapsed so his usual options would be limited. If she took a minute to nail his foot to the floor there's not much he could do.<br /> <br /> It is <i>also</i> entirely possible he did escape that, as in those circumstances a last-second escape would be reasonably within his reach just as well. We didn't see more than a couple minutes into the outcome of her petty revenge on him.</div> </div> </div> </div>The sequence would indicate that he's dead, but we'll see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T23:50:51-07:00","id":1444602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1444480#post1444480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to clarify that I don't mean &quot;Cinder didn't go full Zuko and so I'm sad&quot;, but rather the idea of a villian realizing that team work and co-operation can benefit them and using that for evil was rather nice.<br /> But they had to kill the techy-dapper villian, Penny, toss Neo off a cliff, and scatter everyone.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean Neo was tossed off the same cliff as the protagonists, so if anything it's a good thing for people who want to see more of her.<br /> <br /> That said I suspect that they're going to end up physically visiting the afterlife or something of that nature. Every single character who fell has a connection to some dead character, mostly unresolved ones:<br /> <br /> Ruby: Penny (or Summer, but she never really knew her.)<br /> Yang: Summer<br /> Weiss: Jacques<br /> Blake: Adam<br /> Neo: Roman<br /> Jaune: Pyrrha<br /> <br /> The last two are particularly notable - why send Jaune there? Why did the story go through so many twists to get and keep Neo involved only to drop here there now? Why <i>not</i> any of the other characters? Why kill Jacques now of all times, with no real resolution to his relationships with his daughters? Why bring back Penny only to kill her relatively unceremoniously?<br /> <br /> If we're about to get an arc in the realm of the dead, everything makes sense, and it would answer at least <i>some</i> of the complaints people had (ie. we'll get a bit more closure with Penny, although I doubt any characters actually come back from the dead permanently.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1444598#post1444598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The sequence would indicate that he's dead, but we'll see.</div> </div> </div> </div>We see him smashing a window with a chair, I think, and not much else. But he's a master hacker in the control room of a military filled with airships capable of autonomous flight - if they want him to survive, he'll survive.<br /> <br /> Anyway my main problem with this season was how rapidly and completely they had Ironwood turn into a raving puppy-kicking monster. I feel that they made him too sympathetic previously, then overcorrected in this volume by having him suddenly turn into a complete monster for vaguely-defined reasons. Most of what he's doing here doesn't even help accomplish his goals - it's not even Hard Man Making Hard Decisions, he just murders people and blows up cities to show how evil he is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 04-19-2021, 02:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T10:56:11-07:00","id":1444678,"title":"","content":"It would have worked better if they had worked in his semblance earlier rather than mentioning it in a panel and then assuming everyone knew what it was.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T01:52:38-07:00","id":1445014,"title":"","content":"I definitely sympathise with them having short run times so they obviously have to cut down on certain things or hint towards other things, but I feel Ironwood's semblance was a missed opportunity. It almost feels weird that they chose that since it puts all of his decisions into a very weird context.<br /> <br /> I'm pretty interested to see the next series at this rate, however. I wonder if the Wayforward RWBY game is supposed to be set during V8 or V9?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T00:06:05-07:00","id":1445233,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure it'd be a very satisfying explanation anyway - it's a bit too tailor-made for what it is, and it raises the question of why anyone would have let someone with a Semblance like that end up in a position of power anyway, since it doesn't exactly take deep predictive powers to realize it made him a time bomb waiting to go off.<br /> <br /> Like, we've only seen one other person with a Semblance that is debatably a curse, and nobody would actually put Qrow in charge of anything large-scale (nor would he want it), because it would obviously be a catastrophe. Ironwood's Semblance is even worse - it seems to have no upside whatsoever? I guess you could frame it as a disability and in that respect it might be unfair to him to hold it against him, but surely he's had political enemies throughout his life (he didn't just magically end up in charge from nowhere; it would have been a fight), and surely some of them would have pointed out that his Semblance made him painfully unfit for command.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T00:33:28-07:00","id":1445236,"title":"","content":"There's a thing I've been wondering throughout the recent few seasons and its gonna seem weird. Why are these things happening now? <br /> <br /> Like Salem is out in the open and trying to rule/destroy the world whatever the frack she's doing. But, she's immortal with powers only really comparable by the maidens and lets face it even if you assume each maiden is as strong if not stronger than her as far as raw magic ability goes she's got millenia on them and we've seen her immortality allows her to come back from being obliterated. So why is it just now that she's taken this whole thing public? <br /> <br /> Ironwood's semblance potentially has positive benefits to it, but definitely feels like it was either handled in two ways in universe. A) Something no one knew about in Universe, or B) There was some sort of contingency in place to prevent his semblance to cause him to start quadrupling down on terrible ideas. Heck Ironwood's known about Salem and her being immortal for a long time add what the staff actually does, it kind of astounds me that he doesn't have a room just full of blueprints for various containment modules to shove Salem in till the end of days.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T07:16:34-07:00","id":1445261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1445236#post1445236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a thing I've been wondering throughout the recent few seasons and its gonna seem weird. Why are these things happening now?<br /> <br /> Like Salem is out in the open and trying to rule/destroy the world whatever the frack she's doing. But, she's immortal with powers only really comparable by the maidens and lets face it even if you assume each maiden is as strong if not stronger than her as far as raw magic ability goes she's got millenia on them and we've seen her immortality allows her to come back from being obliterated. So why is it just now that she's taken this whole thing public?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Who knows. The obvious answer is &quot;by and large when she went all out she couldn't quite get her way&quot;. Even in her god-queen days she got defeated by her peer, it didn't stick solely because he's one guy and she kept coming back.<br /> A few failed attempts and a scheming disposition could easily lead to &quot;alright i'd rather do this some other way&quot; outcomes. And she does have a scheming disposition. Always had, even when she went the most ham.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1445236#post1445236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heck Ironwood's known about Salem and her being immortal for a long time add what the staff actually does, it kind of astounds me that he doesn't have a room just full of blueprints for various containment modules to shove Salem in till the end of days.</div> </div> </div> </div> He only knew of her agelessness. Her immunity to being killed is new knowledge. On exploiting the staff to imprison salem... <br /> that's oz's job in the story. He's the one that would have definitely tried it in the literal millennia he's been going at it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":32,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","user":"Synapse","date":". 04-22-2021, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T19:34:17-07:00","id":1445398,"title":"","content":"Penny dying after all that puts me off, I'm not gonna lie, but <i>RWBY </i>isn't finished yet so I'm going to see what happens next.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ironwood's descent into madness works for me, because the man subtly confessed to Team RWBY back in Volume 3 that he sometimes suffers hallucinations.<br /> <br /> HALF of his body was already a prosthetic. Of course this man had PTSD.<br /> <br /> Which only got worse after the Fall of Beacon; remember his hallucination during his first Vault Talk with Oscar?<br /> <br /> I doubt he's been sleeping or eating well since the Fall of Beacon, either. He thinks he's the only one who can save the world, but he also knows the entire world distrusts him right now because someone hacked the robots at Beacon. He's trying to remain neutral in an upcoming election between two people he doesn't want to work with, but SOMEONE is framing him for assassinating supporters of the candidate he would rather work with.<br /> <br /> And then Jacques surprises him by somehow managing to win the election, then rally the council to stand against and interrogate him, then the heating goes out in Mantle, he learns Watts is still alive, Watts is hacking into Atlas itself and taking over everything Ironwood truly cares about, Ironwood flays his remaining arm, he rides the high of thinking he's won, Cinder's queen piece triggers his PTSD from the Fall of Beacon and makes him thinking he's actually stumbled into a trap that will destroy everything, Salem herself appears and toys with his mind, Team RWBY &quot;betrays&quot; him, &quot;Ozpin&quot; &quot;betrays&quot; him, he loses the Winter Maiden so he can't escape, Pietro and Penny &quot;betray&quot; him, he loses Clover, he's STILL not eating or drinking, he has his wounded arm COMPLETELY REMOVED and replaced...<br /> <br /> Salem lets him stew for a bit, then surprises him with a suckerpunch that instantly takes out the shield system he depended on to buy him time to get Penny back, then lands her whale on his precious flying city and starts puking up Grimm. Even if he blows her up now, he has to worry she'll just respawn on the island and there's nothing he can do about it, so he probably doesn't stop to think about that.<br /> <br /> And those damn kids won't stop dooming Atlas in their futile attempts to save a worthless city that cannot be saved. [/bias]<br /> <br /> Ironwood didn't suddenly become evil. He's just progressively going more and more insane, because he's stuck in a Fight or Flight panic, his stress is constantly piling up, and he long ago completely exhausted any mental energy he could use to rally his logical, rational mind. And no one around him can stop his fall because he's surrounded by Yes Men who know he's going to try shooting them in the head.<br /> <br /> It's brilliant tragedy.<br /> <br /> If he had just one day to rest and calm down, he might return to his senses, but that's exactly why Salem never lets up on him but instead constantly maintains and increases pressure.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ozpin doesn't consider his allies to be chess pieces, but Salem absolutely treats this like a game of chess, and she knows that Ironwood is Ozpin's queen piece. He was the one follower with the most institutional influence and military power in the world. So, like a good chess player, Salem carefully planned how to isolate and neutralize Ozpin's queen.<br /> <br /> She kept applying pressure to all of his weaknesses until he CRACKED.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 04-22-2021, 10:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-24T21:23:54-07:00","id":1445779,"title":"","content":"Yup. Most people aggravated with Ironwood's descent is fixating on the fact he always was, even now, an enemy of salem. He's amenable to the crew at the start, because he obviously would be. <br /> <br /> That's nowhere near enough, however, and his descent was, plain and simple, a perfect plan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-25T08:46:59-07:00","id":1445827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1426200-rwby-volume-8-thread?p=1445779#post1445779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup. Most people aggravated with Ironwood's descent is fixating on the fact he always was, even now, an enemy of salem. He's amenable to the crew at the start, because he obviously would be. <br /> <br /> That's nowhere near enough, however, and his descent was, plain and simple, a perfect plan.</div> </div> </div> </div>One should never condemn a person based on their results rather than than their intentions, but good intentions are never enough. The means must justify the ends.<br /> <br /> Ironwood was still, to the end, a better person than Leonardo Lionheart, because as self-centered as Ironwood was, he wasn\u2019t selfish. He was trying to help people to the best of his understanding.<br /> <br /> Aside from his refusal to trust people. <br /> <br /> <br /> And I think most people who think Ironwood\u2019s descent doesn\u2019t make sense are viewing his actions in isolation rather than taking a step back and looking at the entire awful rollercoaster that leads him to each new drop.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}